Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.

If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need
to enable it.  You can execute the following once:

	echo "autoload -U compinit; compinit" >> ~/.zshrc

To load completions in your current shell session:

	source <(cron-person completion zsh)

To load completions for every new session, execute once:

#### Linux:

	cron-person completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_cron-person"

#### macOS:

	cron-person completion zsh > $(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_cron-person

You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.

Usage:
  cron-person completion zsh [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help              help for zsh
      --no-descriptions   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
      --config string   Path to custom configuration file (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string    Path to custom authorization state file (default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
